    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bm0jnub",
      "content": "The Panchayati Raj System represents rural local self-government in India. It aims to decentralize power and ensure people's participation in governance at the grassroots level. The system received constitutional status through the 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act, 1992.<img></img>"
    },
    {
      "type": "statStrip",
      "stats": [
