    {
      "id": "21lkqvr",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Gram Sabha"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "igvz7w3",
      "content": "• Consists of all registered voters in the village."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zp9hzsr",
      "content": "• Acts as the foundation of the Panchayati Raj system."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "hrti8r5",
      "content": "• Approves plans and budgets of the Gram Panchayat."
    },
    {
      "id": "ie0bh7o",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5. Gram Panchayat"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "9obbhgr",
      "content": "• Executive body at village level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "es90qqf",
      "content": "• Members elected directly by villagers."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "je9ttaf",
      "content": "• The head is called Sarpanch or Pradhan."
    },
    {
      "id": "wszo3ff",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "6. Panchayat Samiti"
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Tier / Level",
        "Administrative Level",
        "Key Representative / Head",
        "Primary Functions"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Gram Panchayat",
          "Village Level",
          "Sarpanch / Village Pradhan",
          "Implementation of local village welfare plans, basic infrastructure, and social schemes."
        ],
        [
          "Panchayat Samiti",
          "Block / Intermediate Level",
          "Block Development Officer (BDO) / Chairman",
          "Coordination and aggregation of plans across multiple Gram Panchayats within the block."
        ],
        [
          "Zila Parishad",
          "District Level",
          "District Collector / Zila Parishad Chairperson",
          "District-level policy planning, financial allocation, and oversight of all lower tiers."
        ]
      ],
      "id": "659cgzc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ygocukh",
      "content": "• Works at block level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7u2pya2",
      "content": "• Coordinates activities of Gram Panchayats."
    },
    {
      "id": "khnfb5l",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "7. Zila Parishad"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0lplv28",
      "content": "• Functions at district level."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "zjy67xi",
      "content": "• Supervises Panchayat Samitis."
    },
    {
      "id": "smpiutz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Key Features of the System"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "81bd41e",
      "content": "• Three-tier structure of governance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4ksd1ew",
      "content": "• Regular elections every five years."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "bwxp8xv",
      "content": "• Reservation for SC, ST and women."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "88gneqa",
      "content": "• State Election Commission for conducting elections."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Balwant Rai Mehta Committee (1957) recommended the establishment of a three-tier Panchayati Raj system, and Rajasthan was the first state to adopt it in 1959.",
        "Articles 243 to 243-O under Part IX govern the constitutional provisions of Panchayati Raj, while Schedule 11 lists 29 functional matters.",
        "If a Panchayat is dissolved prematurely, fresh elections must be conducted strictly within six months from the date of dissolution.",
        "Minimum age required to contest Panchayat elections is 21 years (Article 243V)."
      ],
      "id": "n926rai"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "f69zihu",
      "content": "• State Finance Commission for financial review."
    },
    {
      "id": "9vra1ew",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "EXAM Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "aax5gpw",
      "content": "• 73rd Constitutional Amendment Act (1992) introduced Panchayati Raj."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "19qr2h1",
      "content": "• Gram Sabha is the basic unit of rural democracy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kjkptmd",
      "content": "• At least one-third seats reserved for women."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "i0bk397",
      "content": "• Panchayat elections are held every 5 years."
    }
  ],
